.IX Title "OPENSEARCH-GENQUERY 1"
.TH OPENSEARCH-GENQUERY 1 2024-09-09 "perl v5.40.0" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "نام (NAME)"
opensearch\-genquery \- Output the URL of a query generated from an OpenSearch Description
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBopensearch-genquery\fR [\fB\-q\fR] [\fB\-H\fR] [\fB\-A\fR] [\fB\-R\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR\ \fICOUNT\fR] [\fB\-i\fR\ \fIINDEX\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR\ \fIPAGENUM\fR] [\fB\-l\fR\ \fILANG\fR]
[\fB\-O\fR\ \fIENC\fR] [\fB\-I\fR\ \fIENC\fR]
\&\fIURL\fR \fISEARCH\ TERMS...\fR
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Output the URL of a query generated from an OpenSearch Description
file at \fIURL\fR, with the specified \fISEARCH\ TERMS\fR and other
options filled in.
.PP
If multiple search types are available, \fB\-H\fR,
\&\fB\-A\fR and \fB\-R\fR can be used to specify which type is wanted. For
example, \fB\-A\ \-R\fR can be used to request an Atom response, or
failing that fall back to RSS. By default the first URL found in the
description file is used.
.PP
Not all web sites implement all (or any) of the optional OpenSearch
parameters. When used with those sites, the corresponding options will
be silently ignored.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.IX Header "OPTIONS"
.IP \fB\-q\fR 4
.IX Item "-q"
Give no output on errors. In this case, consult the exit code to
determine errors (See "DIAGNOSTICS").
.IP \fB\-H\fR 4
.IX Item "-H"
Request HTML response.
.IP \fB\-A\fR 4
.IX Item "-A"
Request Atom response.
.IP \fB\-R\fR 4
.IX Item "-R"
Request RSS response.
.Sp
\&\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-A\fR, and \fB\-R\fR can be combined to express response type
priority and specify fallback types.
.IP "\fB\-c COUNT\fR, \fB\-\-count=COUNT\fR" 4
.IX Item "-c COUNT, --count=COUNT"
Request COUNT results.
.Sp
OpenSearch parameter: \fIcount\fR.
.IP "\fB\-i INDEX\fR, \fB\-\-startindex=INDEX\fR" 4
.IX Item "-i INDEX, --startindex=INDEX"
Request results start at offset NUM.
.Sp
OpenSearch parameter: \fIstartIndex\fR.
.IP "\fB\-p PAGENUM\fR, \fB\-\-startpage=PAGENUM\fR" 4
.IX Item "-p PAGENUM, --startpage=PAGENUM"
Request results page PAGENUM.
.Sp
OpenSearch parameter: \fIpageIndex\fR.
.IP "\fB\-l LANG\fR, \fB\-\-language=LANG\fR" 4
.IX Item "-l LANG, --language=LANG"
Request results in LANG. LANG should be a 2\-letter ISO country code
(e.g. \fBen\fR or \fBde\fR).
.Sp
OpenSearch parameter: \fIlanguage\fR.
.IP "\fB\-O ENC\fR, \fB\-\-outputencoding=ENC\fR" 4
.IX Item "-O ENC, --outputencoding=ENC"
Request results encoded in ENC (default: UTF\-8).
.Sp
OpenSearch parameter: \fIoutputEncoding\fR.
.IP "\fB\-I ENC\fR, \fB\-\-inputencoding=ENC\fR" 4
.IX Item "-I ENC, --inputencoding=ENC"
Specify search terms are encoded in ENC (default: UTF\-8).
.Sp
OpenSearch parameter: \fIinputEncoding\fR.
.IP "\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR" 4
.IX Item "-h, --help"
Show a short help message.
.IP \fB\-\-\fR 4
.IX Item "--"
End of options.
.SH "عیب‌یابی (DIAGNOSTICS)"
.IX Header "DIAGNOSTICS"
The exit code can be consulted to determine errors, as follows:
.IP "\fB0\fR \- Success." 4
.IX Item "0 - Success."
.PD 0
.IP "\fB1\fR \- Error fetching OpenSearch Description URL." 4
.IX Item "1 - Error fetching OpenSearch Description URL."
.IP "\fB2\fR \- Error parsing OpenSearch Description." 4
.IX Item "2 - Error parsing OpenSearch Description."
.IP "\fB3\fR \- No matching search type found." 4
.IX Item "3 - No matching search type found."
.IP "\fB4\fR \- Cannot find perl module WWW::OpenSearch." 4
.IX Item "4 - Cannot find perl module WWW::OpenSearch."
.IP "\fB5\fR \- Unhandled error from WWW::OpenSearch." 4
.IX Item "5 - Unhandled error from WWW::OpenSearch."
.PD
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.IX Header "DEPENDENCIES"
Requires the module WWW::OpenSearch (Debian package
libwww-opensearch-perl).
.SH "اشکالات (BUGS)"
.IX Header "BUGS"
Only supports GET queries.
.PP
Please report any bugs found to ianb@erislabs.net
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBopensearch\fR\|(1), \fBopensearch\-discover\fR\|(1), \fBsurfraw\fR\|(1),
\&\fBWWW::OpenSearch\fR\|(3pm), <http://www.opensearch.org>
